.TH DWMTERM 1 "September 2026" "dwmterm 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dwmterm \- ultra-minimal, low-latency CPU-framebuffer terminal emulator for DWM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwmterm
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-t\fR \fItitle\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-working\-directory\fR \fIdir\fR]
[\fB\-e\fR \fIcmd\fR [\fIargs...\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dwmterm
(DWM Terminal) is an ultra-minimal, low-latency terminal emulator written in C99
for the X Window System. Designed specifically for seamless integration with
dynamic window managers such as \fBdwm\fR (and \fBdwm-titus\fR),
.B dwmterm
delivers sub-millisecond input responsiveness and a resident memory footprint
under 15 MB RSS.
.PP
Instead of complex GPU pipelines,
.B dwmterm
renders via MIT-SHM shared memory direct CPU framebuffer blits, eliminating
render latency and resource bloat. It features bundled Meslo Nerd Font,
X11 ICCCM/EWMH hints, full DWM window swallowing support, Quickshell ARGB
status-bar icons, an integrated PTY flight recorder ("time machine"), and
built-in Fastfetch and Starship prompt theme presets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d\fR, \fB\-\-working\-directory \fIdir\fR
Set the initial working directory of the spawned shell or command.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR \fIcmd\fR [\fIargs...\fR]
Execute \fIcmd\fR with the given arguments directly in the pseudo-terminal
instead of spawning the default user shell. This option must be specified last
on the command line.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-t\fR \fItitle\fR
Set the initial window title to \fItitle\fR.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-font\-size \fIpt\fR
Set the initial font size in points (6 to 72, default: 12).
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-font \fIfamily\fR
Set the font family name (e.g. "MesloLGS Nerd Font" or "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font").
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-padding \fIpx\fR
Set the internal window padding in pixels (0 to 100, default: 12).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print usage instructions and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B F1
Toggle the Flight Recorder HUD Scrubber ("Time Machine"). When active, use
.B Left
and
.B Right
arrow keys to step backward and forward through your terminal history,
.B Home
to jump to session start, and
.B End
to return to the present. Pressing
.B Escape
or any input key exits scrubber mode.
.TP
.B Ctrl + Plus \fR(\fB=\fR)
Increase font point size at runtime.
.TP
.B Ctrl + Minus \fR(\fB\-\fR)
Decrease font point size at runtime.
.TP
.B Ctrl + 0
Reset font size to the default (12 pt).
.TP
.B Shift + PageUp / Shift + PageDown
Scroll up and down through the scrollback buffer.
.TP
.B Mouse Left Drag
Highlight text to copy to the PRIMARY and CLIPBOARD selections.
.TP
.B Mouse Middle Click
Paste from the PRIMARY selection.
.SH DWM INTEGRATION
.B dwmterm
sets \fBWM_CLASS\fR to:
.RS
.nf
res_name  = "dwmterm"
res_class = "Dwmterm"
.fi
.RE
To enable automatic window swallowing in \fBdwm\fR's \fIconfig.h\fR:
.RS
.nf
/* class      instance    title       tags mask     isfloating   isterminal noswallow monitor */
{ "Dwmterm",  NULL,       NULL,       0,            0,           1,         0,        -1 },
.fi
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Reloads the color palette dynamically from \fI${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/dwmterm/colors\fR
(or \fI~/.config/dwmterm/colors\fR) and immediately repaints all active character cells
and window backgrounds without session interruption.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DWMTERM_DATADIR
Overrides the system data directory for fonts and assets.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dwmterm/config
User configuration file defining typography (font_size, font_family) and initial geometry (cols, rows).
.TP
.I ~/.config/dwmterm/colors.example
Documented template of the default 16-color ANSI palette.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dwmterm/colors
Optional user palette configuration file defining background, foreground, selection,
and ANSI colors 0 through 15.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/fonts/TTF/MesloLGSNerdFont-Regular.ttf
Bundled Meslo Nerd Font installed system-wide via fontconfig.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/dwmterm/fonts/MesloLGSNerdFont-Regular.ttf
Private fallback copy of Meslo Nerd Font.
.SH AUTHORS
Abs and contributors to the Titus DWM project.
